  "descriptions": {
    "preferred": "This dwarf plant is similar to 'Kandy Kitchen' and, like that cultivar, originates from a witches'-broom found and named by Edward Rodd of Raraflora Nursery, Kinterfield, Pennsylvania. The mainly five-lobed small leaves are of the palmatum type, divided up to three-quarter of the way to the leaf base, and are 2. 5-3 cm long and wide. The lobes are ovate with tail-like tips, though the center lobe may be truncated in some leaves. The margins are toothed. The young leaves emerge a bright pink red and become purple red. This color holds well all"
  },
